imneys that we find perform the transformation of smoke into a liquid that we benefit from, and even the water used in the world’s factories, we do not dispose of it in rivers, but rather treat it and benefit from it by chemical methods.\nWe can appreciate and evaluate these writings by their effectiveness in serving the climate crisis and global warming.\n\n\nDo not ask for any honor or appreciation. A person who does these things by inventing them deserves all appreciation, respect, and honor. The Imam is a scholar. I can explain everything written. I just need a translator to translate the language to explain his idea. Thank you very much, and I am grateful.\n\nPeace be upon you. There are smoke extraction devices used in homes, kitchens, and restaurants. Why not add a feature to convert cooking smoke, whether from homes or restaurants, into a liquid and store it in an inconspicuous place, out of reach of children? If possible, this liquid could be utilized and disposed of safely, avoiding dumping it into the soil to prevent soil contamination or groundwater pollution. I can explain all of this if requested.\n\nAnd now, factories worldwide...\n\nPeace be upon you. Is it possible to convert factory smoke into a liquid before it exits the chimneys, separating the liquid into usable substances? Even the water used in factories, instead of being discarded and damaging the land or contaminating groundwater, could be separated and used for other purposes. If we could do this, we would contribute to preventing global warming and climate change, and we could integrate solar energy into everything instead of electricity, creating a harmonious system where it's undetectable as solar-powered, both inside and out. Thank you very much. And gratitude \n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPeace be upon you. It is possible to have the idea of ​​stopping the world's forest fires, but I am not good at English, but I will send a